{"turn": 2, "role": "tool", "result": "**CALVERLEY HERITAGE BANK** 412 Whitaker Street Savannah, Georgia 31401 Telephone: (912) 447-3200\n\n**TERM SHEET --- COMMERCIAL REAL ESTATE LOAN**\n\n**EXECUTED --- FOR BINDING COMMITMENT PURPOSES**\n\n**Date:** April 1, 2025 **Deal Reference:** CHB CRE Loan No. 2025-CHS-0047\n\nThis Term Sheet, when executed by both parties, shall constitute a binding commitment by Lender to fund the Loan described herein, subject to the conditions precedent set forth below. The terms and conditions of the proposed Loan are as follows. This Term Sheet shall expire if not executed by Borrower on or before April 4, 2025.\n\n## SECTION 1: PARTIES\n\n### 1.1 Lender\n\n**Calverley Heritage Bank**, a Georgia state-chartered commercial bank, insured by the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation. EIN: 58-2947136. Principal Office: 412 Whitaker Street, Savannah, Georgia 31401. Primary Contact: Marcus Prideaux, Senior Vice President -- Commercial Real Estate Lending. Telephone: (912) 447-3218. Email: mprideaux@coastalheritagebank.com.\n\n### 1.2 Borrower\n\n**Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC**, a South Carolina limited liability company. South Carolina Secretary of State Filing No.: 2024-0011287. EIN: 84-6213750. Principal Office: 88 Broad Street, Suite 200, Charleston, South Carolina 29401. Registered Agent: Capitol Registered Agents Inc., 1201 Main Street, Suite 410, Columbia, South Carolina 29201. Telephone: (843) 555-0142.\n\n### 1.3 Guarantor / Key Principal\n\n**Neil Ashford Graydon**, an individual, residing at 14 Church Street, Charleston, South Carolina 29401. Mr. Graydon is the managing member and sole owner of Graydon Development Group LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company (the \"Managing Member\"), which owns seventy-two percent (72%) of the membership interests in Borrower. Approximate net worth of Guarantor as of the date hereof: Twenty-Eight Million Dollars (\\$28,000,000).\n\n### 1.4 Other Members of Borrower\n\nThe membership interests in Borrower are held as follows:\n\n  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  Member                                                                                           Jurisdiction         Interest        Role\n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ -------------------- --------------- -----------------\n  Graydon Development Group LLC (\"GDG\")                                                            South Carolina LLC   72%             Managing Member\n\n  Tidewater Opportunity Fund II LP (\"Tidewater\") (GP: Tidewater GP Holdings LLC, a Delaware LLC)   Delaware LP          18%             Passive Member\n\n  Harborline Capital Advisors LLC (\"Harborline\")                                                   Delaware LLC         10%             Passive Member\n\n  **Total**                                                                                                             **100%**        \n  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## SECTION 2: PROPERTY\n\n### 2.1 Property Description\n\nThe real property located at and commonly known as 520--534 King Street, Charleston, South Carolina 29403 (the \"Property\"), more particularly described as follows:\n\nLots 7, 8, and 9 of the Hampstead Village Plat, as recorded in Plat Book 41 at Page 218 in the Office of the Register of Mesne Conveyances (\"RMC Office\") for Charleston County, South Carolina, together with that certain strip of land formerly known as Anson Lane, vacated by City of Charleston Ordinance No. 2019-084, and conveyed to the predecessor in title by quitclaim deed recorded in Deed Book 1128 at Page 443 in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina.\n\nCharleston County Tax Map Nos.: 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009.\n\nA summary legal description is attached hereto as **Exhibit A**. The full legal description shall be confirmed from the title commitment and ALTA/NSPS survey and incorporated into the Mortgage and Security Agreement.\n\n### 2.2 Property Type and Improvements\n\nThe Property is improved with a mixed-use commercial building containing ground-floor retail and upper-floor office space. The improvements consist of three (3) retail bays totaling approximately 11,400 square feet on the ground floor and two (2) office suites totaling approximately 19,600 square feet on the upper two floors. Total gross building area: approximately 31,000 square feet. Land area: approximately 0.38 acres (16,553 square feet). The Property is located within the GB (General Business) zoning district of the City of Charleston. Original construction occurred in 1952, with a significant renovation completed in 2004.\n\n### 2.3 Existing Tenancies\n\nCurrent occupancy is approximately sixty-eight percent (68%). The existing tenancies are summarized in the following table:\n\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  Unit              Area (SF)    Tenant                            Use                 Lease Type       Rent/SF   Annual Rent     Expiration\n  ----------------- ------------ --------------------------------- ------------------- ---------------- --------- --------------- ------------\n  Bay 1             3,800        Lowcountry Provisions Inc.        Specialty Grocery   NNN              \\$28.50   \\$108,300       12/31/2027\n\n  Bay 2             3,800        *VACANT*                          ---                 ---              ---       ---             ---\n\n  Bay 3             3,800        Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC   Interior Design     Modified Gross   \\$24.00   \\$91,200        06/30/2026\n\n  2nd Fl. Suite A   9,800        Tidemark Consulting Group LLC     Mgmt. Consulting    NNN              \\$22.00   \\$215,600       03/31/2029\n\n  2nd Fl. Suite B   9,800        *VACANT*                          ---                 ---              ---       ---             ---\n\n  **Total**         **31,000**                                                                                    **\\$415,100**   \n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTotal In-Place Annual Rent: Four Hundred Fifteen Thousand One Hundred Dollars (\\$415,100). Vacant space consists of Bay 2 (3,800 SF) and 2nd Floor Suite B (9,800 SF), totaling 13,600 square feet, or approximately 43.9% of total building area. Estoppel certificates and subordination, non-disturbance, and attornment agreements (\"SNDAs\") shall be required from all existing tenants as a condition precedent to closing.\n\n### 2.4 Appraised Value\n\nAn appraisal of the Property has been completed by Pinnacle Valuation Services LLC, dated February 14, 2025, in accordance with the Uniform Standards of Professional Appraisal Practice (\"USPAP\") and the requirements of Title XI of the Financial Institutions Reform, Recovery, and Enforcement Act of 1989 (\"FIRREA\"). The appraised values are as follows:\n\n- **As-Is Value:** \\$18,200,000\n- **As-Stabilized Value** (assuming 95% occupancy and completion of planned renovation): \\$23,500,000\n\n## SECTION 3: LOAN TERMS\n\n### 3.1 Loan Amount\n\n**Fourteen Million Seven Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$14,750,000).**\n\n### 3.2 Loan Purpose\n\nAcquisition and renovation of the Property. The agreed purchase price for the Property is Seventeen Million Eight Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$17,800,000).\n\n### 3.3 Initial Advance and Renovation Holdback\n\nThe Loan proceeds shall be disbursed as follows:\n\n**(a) Initial Advance at Closing:** Twelve Million Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$12,500,000), to be applied toward the purchase price, closing costs, and funded reserves.\n\n**(b) Renovation Holdback:** Two Million Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$2,250,000) (being \\$14,750,000 minus \\$12,500,000), to be held by Lender and disbursed on a draw basis for renovation costs upon satisfaction of the conditions and procedures described in Sections 6.4 and 8 of this Term Sheet.\n\nThe total renovation budget for the Property is Three Million One Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$3,150,000), as set forth in Section 3.4 below and Exhibit B. Borrower shall be responsible for renovation costs in excess of the Renovation Holdback from Borrower's own funds.\n\n### 3.4 Total Project Cost and Borrower Equity\n\nThe total cost of the acquisition and renovation of the Property (the \"Total Project Cost\") is estimated as follows:\n\n  -------------------------------------------------------------\n  Component                      Amount\n  ------------------------------ ------------------------------\n  Purchase Price                 \\$17,800,000\n\n  Renovation Budget              \\$3,150,000\n\n  **Total Project Cost**         **\\$20,950,000**\n  -------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Borrower Equity Contribution:** Six Million Two Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$6,200,000), representing approximately 29.6% of the Total Project Cost.\n\nThe renovation budget is comprised of the following components:\n\n  --------------------------------------------------------------\n  Line Item                       Amount\n  ------------------------------- ------------------------------\n  HVAC Replacement                \\$1,200,000\n\n  Elevator Modernization          \\$475,000\n\n  Façade Restoration              \\$625,000\n\n  Tenant Improvement Allowances   \\$550,000\n\n  Soft Costs and Contingency      \\$300,000\n\n  **Total Renovation Budget**     **\\$3,150,000**\n  --------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe general contractor for the renovation shall be Beaufort Builders Group LLC, South Carolina General Contractor License No. SC-GC-47921. The executed construction contract between Borrower and Beaufort Builders Group LLC provides for a contract sum of Two Million Eight Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$2,850,000) covering hard costs of construction. The balance of Three Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$300,000) for soft costs and contingency is outside the scope of the general contractor agreement.\n\n### 3.5 Loan Metrics\n\nThe key loan metrics for this transaction are as follows:\n\n- **Loan-to-Value (As-Is):** \\$14,750,000 / \\$18,200,000 = approximately 81%\n- **Loan-to-Value (As-Stabilized):** \\$14,750,000 / \\$23,500,000 = 62.77%\n- **Loan-to-Cost:** \\$14,750,000 / \\$20,950,000 = 70.41%\n\n### 3.6 Interest Rate\n\nThe Loan shall bear interest at a floating rate equal to Daily SOFR plus two hundred eighty-five basis points (2.85%) per annum. \"Daily SOFR\" shall mean the Secured Overnight Financing Rate as published by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York (or a successor administrator) on the applicable business day, or if such rate is not published on such business day, the rate published on the immediately preceding business day.\n\n**SOFR Floor:** The applicable SOFR rate for purposes of calculating the interest rate on the Loan shall not be less than three percent (3.00%) per annum. In the event that Daily SOFR is less than 3.00%, the interest rate on the Loan shall be calculated using a SOFR rate of 3.00%.\n\n### 3.7 Default Rate\n\nUpon the occurrence and during the continuance of an Event of Default, the outstanding principal balance of the Loan shall bear interest at a rate equal to the otherwise applicable interest rate plus five percent (5.00%) per annum (the \"Default Rate\"). Interest at the Default Rate shall accrue from the date of the Event of Default until such Event of Default is cured or the Loan is repaid in full, whichever first occurs.\n\n### 3.8 Maturity Date\n\nThe Loan shall have a term of five (5) years from the date of closing. Based on the anticipated closing date of April 15, 2025, the Maturity Date shall be **April 15, 2030**. The entire outstanding principal balance, together with all accrued and unpaid interest and any other amounts due under the Loan Documents, shall be due and payable on the Maturity Date.\n\n### 3.9 Amortization\n\nThe Loan shall be interest-only for the first twenty-four (24) months from the date of closing (the \"Interest-Only Period\"), commencing on the first Payment Date and ending on or about April 15, 2027. During the Interest-Only Period, monthly payments shall consist solely of accrued interest on the outstanding principal balance.\n\nThereafter, commencing with the payment due on May 15, 2027, and continuing through the Maturity Date, monthly payments of principal and interest shall be due based on a twenty-five (25) year amortization schedule, calculated using the then-outstanding principal balance and the then-applicable interest rate. The remaining unpaid principal balance, together with all accrued and unpaid interest and any other amounts due, shall be due and payable in full on the Maturity Date.\n\n### 3.10 Payment Date\n\nAll payments of principal and interest shall be due and payable monthly, on the fifteenth (15th) day of each calendar month, commencing May 15, 2025.\n\n### 3.11 Late Charge\n\nA late charge equal to five percent (5%) of any monthly installment of principal and/or interest shall be assessed on any payment not received by Lender within ten (10) calendar days of the applicable due date. The late charge is intended to compensate Lender for the additional administrative expense of processing late payments and shall not be deemed a penalty.\n\n## SECTION 4: PREPAYMENT\n\n### 4.1 Lockout Period\n\nThe Loan may not be prepaid, in whole or in part, during the first twenty-four (24) months from the date of closing (the \"Lockout Period\"). No voluntary prepayments of principal shall be permitted during the Lockout Period, and any prepayment made in violation of this restriction shall be subject to a prepayment premium as described in Section 4.2 below.\n\n### 4.2 Yield Maintenance Period\n\nFrom the expiration of the Lockout Period through the forty-eighth (48th) month from closing (i.e., months 25 through 48), the Loan may be prepaid in whole (but not in part) upon not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Lender, and upon simultaneous payment of a yield maintenance premium (the \"Yield Maintenance Premium\") equal to the greater of:\n\n**(a)** one percent (1.00%) of the outstanding principal balance of the Loan as of the date of prepayment; or\n\n**(b)** the present value of the excess of (i) the interest that would have accrued on the prepaid principal amount at the applicable Note rate for the period from the date of prepayment through the end of the forty-eighth (48th) month from closing, over (ii) the interest that would accrue on such prepaid principal amount at the treasury rate plus fifty (50) basis points for such remaining period, discounted to present value at the treasury rate.\n\nThe Yield Maintenance Premium, if any, shall be due and payable together with the full prepayment of the outstanding principal balance, all accrued and unpaid interest, and any other amounts due under the Loan Documents. Partial prepayments shall not be permitted during the Yield Maintenance Period.\n\n### 4.3 Open Prepayment Period\n\nDuring the final twelve (12) months of the Loan term (i.e., months 49 through 60), the Loan may be prepaid in whole or in part, at any time and from time to time, without payment of any prepayment premium, penalty, or yield maintenance amount, upon not less than fifteen (15) days' prior written notice to Lender.\n\n## SECTION 5: COLLATERAL AND SECURITY\n\n### 5.1 Mortgage and Security Agreement\n\nThe Loan shall be secured by a first-priority mortgage lien on the Property (including all three tax parcels and the vacated Anson Lane strip described in Section 2.1), encumbering and covering the following:\n\n(a) the fee simple interest in the Property, including the land, all improvements, and all appurtenances thereto;\n\n(b) all buildings, structures, fixtures, and building systems now or hereafter located on or affixed to the Property, including without limitation all HVAC equipment, elevators, plumbing, electrical systems, and fire protection systems;\n\n(c) all personal property, equipment, furniture, furnishings, and trade fixtures owned by Borrower and used in connection with the operation of the Property;\n\n(d) all deposits, accounts, reserves, and escrows established in connection with the Loan;\n\n(e) all insurance proceeds, condemnation awards, and other payments arising from the damage, destruction, or taking of the Property or any portion thereof;\n\n(f) all permits, licenses, entitlements, approvals, development rights, and governmental authorizations relating to the Property;\n\n(g) all contracts, warranties, guarantees, indemnities, and claims relating to the construction, renovation, operation, or maintenance of the Property, including without limitation Borrower's interest in the renovation contract with Beaufort Builders Group LLC; and\n\n(h) all leases, rents, issues, profits, revenues, and other income derived from the Property.\n\nThe Mortgage and Security Agreement shall be prepared by Lender's counsel and recorded in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina.\n\n### 5.2 Assignment of Leases and Rents\n\nBorrower shall execute and deliver an absolute assignment of all leases, rents, profits, revenues, and other income from the Property in favor of Lender. The assignment of leases and rents may be included within the Mortgage and Security Agreement or executed as a separate instrument, at the discretion of Lender's counsel. If executed as a separate instrument, it shall be recorded in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina.\n\n### 5.3 UCC Financing Statement\n\nBorrower shall execute and deliver a UCC-1 financing statement to be filed with the South Carolina Secretary of State, covering all personal property collateral, fixtures, and as-extracted collateral (if any) described in the Mortgage and Security Agreement. Continuation statements and amendments shall be filed as necessary to maintain the perfection of Lender's security interest throughout the term of the Loan.\n\n### 5.4 Environmental Indemnity Agreement\n\nBorrower and Guarantor shall execute and deliver a separate environmental indemnity agreement in favor of Lender, in form and substance satisfactory to Lender and Lender's counsel, indemnifying and holding Lender harmless from and against any and all losses, liabilities, damages, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising from or relating to the presence, release, or threatened release of hazardous substances on, under, or emanating from the Property.\n\n### 5.5 Guaranty\n\nNeil Ashford Graydon (\"Guarantor\") shall execute and deliver a full recourse personal guaranty in favor of Lender, structured as follows:\n\n**(a) Non-Recourse Carve-Out Guaranty.** The Loan shall be structured as non-recourse to Borrower, except for certain \"carve-out\" events (commonly referred to as \"bad boy\" acts) that trigger springing full recourse liability of Guarantor for the entire outstanding indebtedness. Such carve-out events shall include, without limitation: (i) fraud or intentional misrepresentation by Borrower or Guarantor; (ii) misapplication or misappropriation of rents, security deposits, insurance proceeds, or condemnation awards; (iii) voluntary bankruptcy filing by or on behalf of Borrower; (iv) environmental liability arising from the acts or omissions of Borrower, Guarantor, or their agents; and (v) violation of the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 10.3 of this Term Sheet.\n\n**(b) Completion Guaranty.** Guarantor shall unconditionally guarantee the completion of the renovation scope described in Section 8 within the approved renovation budget and by the Substantial Completion Deadline set forth in Section 8.3.\n\n**(c) Payment Guaranty --- Interest Shortfall.** Guarantor shall guarantee payment of any shortfall in debt service payments during the renovation and initial lease-up period, covering the first fourteen (14) months following closing, to the extent that net operating income from the Property is insufficient to cover monthly interest payments during such period.\n\n### 5.6 Title Insurance\n\nLender shall receive, at Borrower's expense, an ALTA Lender's title insurance policy in the amount of Fourteen Million Seven Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$14,750,000), issued by Commonwealth National Title Underwriters Inc. through Prestige Title & Settlement Services LLC (Title Commitment No. PT-2025-04-1178, effective date February 28, 2025), insuring the first-priority lien of the Mortgage and Security Agreement, subject only to those exceptions approved by Lender in writing (\"Permitted Exceptions\"). Borrower shall also obtain such endorsements as Lender may reasonably require, including without limitation zoning, access, survey, comprehensive, and future advance endorsements.\n\n## SECTION 6: RESERVE AND ESCROW REQUIREMENTS\n\n### 6.1 Tax and Insurance Escrow\n\nBorrower shall make monthly deposits with Lender in an amount equal to one-twelfth (1/12) of the estimated annual real property taxes and casualty and liability insurance premiums for the Property, covering all three tax parcels (Tax Map Nos. 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009). Such deposits shall be held by Lender in escrow and applied by Lender toward the payment of real property taxes and insurance premiums as they become due and payable. Lender shall have the right to adjust the monthly escrow amount periodically based on actual or anticipated tax assessments and insurance premiums.\n\n### 6.2 Capital Replacement Reserve\n\nBorrower shall make monthly deposits with Lender in the amount of Six Hundred Forty-Five Dollars and Eighty-Three Cents (\\$645.83) into a capital replacement reserve account, calculated as follows: \\$0.25 per square foot per year multiplied by 31,000 square feet of gross building area, equaling \\$7,750 per year, divided by twelve (12) months. Funds in the capital replacement reserve shall be disbursed to Borrower upon Lender's approval of qualifying capital expenditures, subject to Lender's reasonable review and approval procedures.\n\n### 6.3 Tenant Improvement / Leasing Commission Reserve\n\nBorrower shall deposit at closing the sum of One Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$150,000) into a tenant improvement and leasing commission reserve account held by Lender. Upon any draw-down from such reserve, Borrower shall replenish the reserve to the full amount of \\$150,000 from Borrower's own funds within thirty (30) days of Lender's written demand. Disbursements from the reserve shall be subject to Lender's prior written approval and shall be used exclusively for tenant improvement costs and leasing commissions incurred in connection with the leasing of vacant space at the Property.\n\n### 6.4 Renovation Reserve (Holdback)\n\nTwo Million Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$2,250,000) of the total Loan commitment shall be held by Lender as a renovation reserve (the \"Renovation Holdback\") and disbursed to Borrower on a draw basis for renovation costs incurred at the Property. Disbursements from the Renovation Holdback shall be made upon Lender's receipt of a draw request accompanied by:\n\n(i) a certification from Borrower's architect that the work for which payment is requested has been completed in accordance with the approved plans and specifications;\n\n(ii) partial lien waivers from the general contractor and all subcontractors performing work for which payment is requested; and\n\n(iii) a title endorsement (date-down) from the title insurer confirming no intervening liens or encumbrances on the Property since the date of the Mortgage recording or the most recent date-down endorsement.\n\nBorrower shall be responsible for renovation costs in excess of the Renovation Holdback from Borrower's own funds. Additional conditions and procedures for disbursement of the Renovation Holdback are set forth in Section 8.4 of this Term Sheet.\n\n## SECTION 7: FINANCIAL COVENANTS AND REPORTING\n\n### 7.1 Debt Service Coverage Ratio\n\nBorrower shall maintain a minimum Debt Service Coverage Ratio (\"DSCR\") of not less than **1.25x**. DSCR testing shall commence twenty-four (24) months after the date of closing, with the first test date to be the first full calendar quarter ending after the twenty-fourth month following closing (anticipated to be approximately July 15, 2027, for the quarter ending June 30, 2027). Thereafter, DSCR shall be tested on a quarterly basis.\n\nFor purposes of this Term Sheet, \"DSCR\" shall mean Net Operating Income divided by Annual Debt Service. The precise definitions of \"Net Operating Income\" and \"Annual Debt Service\" shall be set forth in the Loan Documents, as prepared by Lender's counsel.\n\n### 7.2 Net Worth and Liquidity Covenants\n\nBorrower shall maintain at all times during the term of the Loan:\n\n**(a)** a net worth of not less than One Million Dollars (\\$1,000,000); and\n\n**(b)** liquid assets (defined as cash, cash equivalents, marketable securities, and unencumbered deposits held at federally insured depository institutions) of not less than Five Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$500,000).\n\nCompliance with the net worth and liquidity covenants shall be tested annually based on the financial statements and certifications delivered pursuant to Section 7.3.\n\n### 7.3 Financial Reporting Requirements\n\nBorrower and Guarantor shall provide the following financial information and reports to Lender:\n\n**(a)** Annual audited financial statements of Borrower, prepared in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles (\"GAAP\") by an independent certified public accounting firm acceptable to Lender, to be delivered within one hundred twenty (120) days of the end of Borrower's fiscal year;\n\n**(b)** Annual personal financial statement of Guarantor, in form and detail satisfactory to Lender, to be delivered within one hundred twenty (120) days of the end of each calendar year;\n\n**(c)** Quarterly rent rolls for the Property, certified by Borrower as true, correct, and complete, to be delivered within thirty (30) days of the end of each calendar quarter;\n\n**(d)** Annual property operating statements for the Property, including a detailed income and expense report and comparison to budget, to be delivered within one hundred twenty (120) days of the end of Borrower's fiscal year; and\n\n**(e)** Copies of all lease agreements and lease modifications executed by Borrower with respect to the Property, to be delivered to Lender within ten (10) business days of execution.\n\n## SECTION 8: RENOVATION / CONSTRUCTION PROVISIONS\n\n### 8.1 General Contractor\n\nThe general contractor for the renovation of the Property shall be **Beaufort Builders Group LLC**, South Carolina General Contractor License No. SC-GC-47921. Principal Office: 2200 Boundary Street, Suite 150, Beaufort, South Carolina 29902. The contract sum under the executed construction contract between Borrower and Beaufort Builders Group LLC is Two Million Eight Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$2,850,000), covering hard costs of construction. Borrower shall provide Lender with a complete copy of the executed construction contract and all amendments, change orders, or modifications thereto prior to closing.\n\n### 8.2 Renovation Budget\n\nThe total renovation budget for the Property is Three Million One Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$3,150,000), comprised of the following line items:\n\n  --------------------------------------------------------------\n  Line Item                       Amount\n  ------------------------------- ------------------------------\n  HVAC Replacement                \\$1,200,000\n\n  Elevator Modernization          \\$475,000\n\n  Façade Restoration              \\$625,000\n\n  Tenant Improvement Allowances   \\$550,000\n\n  Soft Costs and Contingency      \\$300,000\n\n  **Total Renovation Budget**     **\\$3,150,000**\n  --------------------------------------------------------------\n\nA detailed renovation budget summary is attached hereto as **Exhibit B**.\n\n### 8.3 Substantial Completion Deadline\n\nRenovation of the Property shall be substantially completed within fourteen (14) months from the date of closing. Based on the anticipated closing date of April 15, 2025, the Substantial Completion Deadline shall be **June 15, 2026**. \"Substantial completion\" shall mean the completion of all renovation work in accordance with the approved plans and specifications, as certified by Borrower's architect, and the issuance of a certificate of occupancy (or equivalent) by the City of Charleston for the renovated portions of the Property.\n\n### 8.4 Draw Procedures\n\nDraws from the Renovation Holdback shall be made no more frequently than once per calendar month. Each draw request submitted by Borrower shall include the following:\n\n**(i)** an AIA G702/G703 Application and Certificate for Payment, certified by Borrower's architect of record, detailing the work completed, amounts previously paid, and the amount currently requested;\n\n**(ii)** lien waivers from the general contractor and all subcontractors performing work in an amount exceeding Twenty-Five Thousand Dollars (\\$25,000) --- conditional lien waivers for the current draw and unconditional lien waivers for all prior draws;\n\n**(iii)** a title date-down endorsement from the title insurer confirming that no intervening mechanic's liens, materialmen's liens, or other encumbrances have been filed against the Property since the date of the most recent title endorsement; and\n\n**(iv)** evidence of Lender's satisfactory inspection of the work in progress, which inspection may be conducted by a third-party inspector retained by Lender at Borrower's expense.\n\nLender shall retain ten percent (10%) retainage from each disbursement from the Renovation Holdback until substantial completion of the renovation has been achieved in accordance with Section 8.3. Retainage shall be released upon Lender's receipt of satisfactory evidence of substantial completion, final lien waivers from all contractors and subcontractors, and a final title date-down endorsement. Lender shall have no obligation to disburse any portion of the Renovation Holdback if an Event of Default has occurred and is continuing under the Loan Documents.\n\n## SECTION 9: INSURANCE REQUIREMENTS\n\n### 9.1 Property Insurance\n\nBorrower shall maintain at all times during the term of the Loan comprehensive all-risk property insurance covering the Property and all improvements thereon, on a replacement cost basis, with an agreed amount endorsement (waiver of coinsurance). The policy shall name Lender as mortgagee and loss payee pursuant to a standard mortgagee clause. Coverage shall include, without limitation, fire, windstorm, hail, explosion, vandalism, malicious mischief, and such other perils as Lender may reasonably require.\n\n### 9.2 Commercial General Liability\n\nBorrower shall maintain commercial general liability insurance with minimum coverage limits of Two Million Dollars (\\$2,000,000) per occurrence and Five Million Dollars (\\$5,000,000) in the aggregate. Lender shall be named as an additional insured on such policy. The policy shall include coverage for premises liability, operations liability, products and completed operations, and personal and advertising injury.\n\n### 9.3 Flood Insurance\n\nBorrower shall maintain flood insurance on the Property in an amount not less than Five Million Dollars (\\$5,000,000). The Property is located in FEMA Flood Zone X. Notwithstanding that flood insurance may not be required by federal regulation for properties in Zone X, Lender requires flood insurance coverage as a condition of this Loan. The flood insurance policy shall name Lender as mortgagee and loss payee.\n\n### 9.4 Builder's Risk Insurance\n\nDuring the renovation period (from closing through substantial completion of the renovation), Borrower shall maintain builder's risk insurance in an amount not less than the full renovation budget of Three Million One Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$3,150,000), covering the Property and the renovation work against all risks of physical loss or damage during the course of construction. Lender shall be named as mortgagee and loss payee on such policy.\n\n### 9.5 Other Insurance\n\nBorrower shall maintain the following additional insurance coverages:\n\n**(a)** Workers' compensation insurance in the amounts required by the laws of the State of South Carolina, covering all employees of Borrower and, to the extent not covered under the general contractor's policies, all persons engaged in the renovation of the Property;\n\n**(b)** Umbrella/excess liability insurance in an amount not less than Five Million Dollars (\\$5,000,000), providing excess coverage over the commercial general liability, automobile liability, and employers' liability policies; and\n\n**(c)** Such other insurance coverages as Lender may reasonably require from time to time, in amounts and with carriers acceptable to Lender.\n\nAll insurance policies required under this Section 9 shall be issued by insurers licensed to do business in the State of South Carolina, having an A.M. Best rating of not less than A-:VII, and shall contain a provision requiring not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Lender of cancellation, non-renewal, or material modification.\n\n## SECTION 10: AFFIRMATIVE AND NEGATIVE COVENANTS\n\n### 10.1 Single-Purpose Entity\n\nBorrower shall at all times maintain its status as a single-purpose entity (\"SPE\"). The SPE covenants shall include, without limitation, the following requirements:\n\n**(a)** Borrower shall not engage in any business or activity other than the ownership, operation, renovation, leasing, management, and disposition of the Property and activities incidental thereto;\n\n**(b)** Borrower shall maintain its own separate books of account, financial records, and bank accounts, separate and apart from those of any other person or entity;\n\n**(c)** Borrower shall not commingle its funds or assets with those of any affiliate, member, manager, or other person or entity;\n\n**(d)** Borrower shall hold itself out to the public as a legal entity separate and distinct from any other person or entity, including its members and affiliates, and shall conduct its business in its own name;\n\n**(e)** Borrower shall maintain adequate capitalization in light of its contemplated business operations, transactions, and liabilities;\n\n**(f)** Borrower shall not incur any additional indebtedness, whether secured or unsecured, without the prior written consent of Lender; and\n\n**(g)** Borrower's organizational documents, including its operating agreement and certificate of formation, shall be amended, to the extent necessary, to include these restrictions and covenants prior to closing.\n\n### 10.2 No Subordinate Financing\n\nBorrower shall not incur, create, assume, or permit to exist any subordinate lien, mortgage, security interest, encumbrance, or indebtedness secured by the Property or any portion thereof, without the prior written consent of Lender. This restriction shall apply to all forms of indebtedness, including without limitation mezzanine loans, preferred equity interests, and any other financing arrangements that may affect Lender's collateral position.\n\n### 10.3 Transfer Restrictions\n\nBorrower shall not, without Lender's prior written consent, sell, convey, transfer, assign, pledge, encumber, or otherwise dispose of any interest in the Property. Additionally, no transfer of ownership interests in the Borrower exceeding ten percent (10%) individually or twenty-five percent (25%) in the aggregate shall be permitted without Lender's prior written consent, except for transfers among the existing members of Borrower.\n\nAny transfer in violation of this Section 10.3 shall constitute an Event of Default under the Loan Documents and may trigger the acceleration of the outstanding indebtedness, the imposition of the Default Rate, and the exercise of all remedies available to Lender under the Loan Documents and applicable law.\n\n### 10.4 Compliance with Laws\n\nBorrower shall at all times comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws, rules, regulations, orders, ordinances, and governmental requirements applicable to the Property and the conduct of Borrower's business, including without limitation all zoning, building, fire, health, safety, and environmental laws and regulations.\n\n### 10.5 Maintenance and Repairs\n\nBorrower shall maintain the Property, including all improvements, fixtures, building systems, and common areas, in good order, condition, and repair, consistent with the standards of comparable mixed-use commercial properties in the Charleston, South Carolina metropolitan area. Borrower shall not commit or permit any waste of the Property or any portion thereof.\n\n### 10.6 Leasing Covenant\n\nBorrower shall use commercially reasonable efforts to lease all vacant space at the Property at market rents and on terms consistent with those prevailing for comparable mixed-use commercial properties in the Charleston, South Carolina metropolitan area, and on terms reasonably acceptable to Lender. All new leases and all lease modifications for spaces in excess of five thousand (5,000) square feet or for lease terms exceeding five (5) years shall require the prior written consent of Lender, which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld, conditioned, or delayed.\n\n## SECTION 11: EVENTS OF DEFAULT\n\n### 11.1 Events of Default\n\nEach of the following shall constitute an \"Event of Default\" under the Loan Documents:\n\n**(a)** Failure by Borrower to make any payment of principal, interest, or any other amount due under the Loan Documents when due, subject to the cure period set forth in Section 11.2;\n\n**(b)** Breach by Borrower of any covenant, agreement, or obligation contained in the Loan Documents or this Term Sheet, continuing beyond the applicable cure period set forth in Section 11.2;\n\n**(c)** Any representation or warranty made by Borrower or Guarantor in connection with the Loan or in any Loan Document that proves to be materially false, misleading, or inaccurate in any material respect when made or deemed made;\n\n**(d)** The filing of a petition in bankruptcy by or against Borrower or Guarantor, or the appointment of a receiver, trustee, or custodian for any substantial part of the property or assets of Borrower or Guarantor, or any assignment for the benefit of creditors by Borrower or Guarantor, or any similar insolvency proceeding;\n\n**(e)** A default by Borrower or Guarantor under any other indebtedness for borrowed money in an amount exceeding Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars (\\$250,000), individually or in the aggregate, which default is not cured within any applicable cure or grace period;\n\n**(f)** Failure by Borrower to maintain any insurance required under Section 9 of this Term Sheet or the Loan Documents;\n\n**(g)** Violation of the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 10.3;\n\n**(h)** Failure by Borrower to achieve substantial completion of the renovation by the Substantial Completion Deadline set forth in Section 8.3;\n\n**(i)** The DSCR falling below 1.25x for two (2) consecutive calendar quarters following the commencement of DSCR testing as set forth in Section 7.1, without cure;\n\n**(j)** Breach of any SPE covenant set forth in Section 10.1;\n\n**(k)** A material adverse change in the financial condition, business, assets, or operations of Borrower or Guarantor that, in Lender's reasonable judgment, materially impairs the ability of Borrower to perform its obligations under the Loan Documents or of Guarantor to perform its obligations under the Guaranty Agreement; and\n\n**(l)** The occurrence of any other event or condition that constitutes an Event of Default as defined in the Loan Documents.\n\n### 11.2 Cure Periods\n\nThe following cure periods shall apply to the Events of Default described in Section 11.1:\n\n**(a) Payment Defaults:** Five (5) business days from the date on which payment was due.\n\n**(b) Non-Monetary Defaults** (other than SPE defaults, transfer restriction defaults, and insurance defaults): Thirty (30) calendar days after written notice from Lender to Borrower of such default; provided, however, that if the default is of a nature that it cannot reasonably be cured within thirty (30) calendar days and Borrower has commenced and is diligently pursuing the cure thereof, the cure period shall be extended for an additional period not to exceed sixty (60) calendar days (for a total cure period not to exceed ninety (90) calendar days).\n\n**(c) SPE and Transfer Defaults:** No cure period. Any breach of the SPE covenants set forth in Section 10.1 or the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 10.3 shall constitute an immediate Event of Default without notice or opportunity to cure.\n\n## SECTION 12: CONDITIONS PRECEDENT TO CLOSING\n\n### 12.1 Conditions\n\nThe obligation of Lender to close the Loan and advance the initial disbursement of Loan proceeds shall be subject to the satisfaction of each of the following conditions precedent, each in form and substance satisfactory to Lender and Lender's counsel:\n\n**(a)** Execution and delivery of all Loan Documents, including without limitation the Promissory Note, Mortgage and Security Agreement, Assignment of Leases and Rents, Environmental Indemnity Agreement, Guaranty Agreement, and UCC-1 Financing Statement;\n\n**(b)** Receipt by Lender of a satisfactory title commitment and pro forma lender's title insurance policy from Prestige Title & Settlement Services LLC and Commonwealth National Title Underwriters Inc. (Commitment No. PT-2025-04-1178), showing fee simple ownership of the Property vested in Borrower, subject only to Permitted Exceptions approved by Lender, and committing to insure the first-priority lien of the Mortgage in the amount of \\$14,750,000;\n\n**(c)** Receipt by Lender of a satisfactory Phase I Environmental Site Assessment from Clearfield Environmental Consulting LLC (Report No. CLR-2025-0119, dated January 28, 2025), indicating no recognized environmental conditions requiring remediation or further investigation, unless otherwise acceptable to Lender;\n\n**(d)** Receipt by Lender of a satisfactory appraisal from Pinnacle Valuation Services LLC (dated February 14, 2025), conforming to the requirements of USPAP and FIRREA, and supporting the as-is and as-stabilized values set forth in Section 2.4;\n\n**(e)** Receipt by Lender of a current ALTA/NSPS Land Title Survey of the Property, prepared by a surveyor licensed in the State of South Carolina, satisfactory in form and content to Lender and the title insurer;\n\n**(f)** Evidence of all required insurance policies described in Section 9, with certificates of insurance naming Lender as mortgagee, loss payee, and/or additional insured, as applicable;\n\n**(g)** Delivery to Lender of Borrower's organizational documents, including its operating agreement, certificate of formation, and certificates of good standing from the South Carolina Secretary of State and the secretary of state of each other jurisdiction in which Borrower is qualified to do business, all satisfactory to Lender and Lender's counsel;\n\n**(h)** Delivery to Lender of legal opinions of Borrower's counsel, addressed to Lender, in form and substance satisfactory to Lender's counsel, opining as to: (i) the due organization, valid existence, and good standing of Borrower; (ii) the due authorization and valid execution of the Loan Documents by Borrower; (iii) the enforceability of the Loan Documents against Borrower; and (iv) the absence of conflicts with Borrower's organizational documents, applicable law, or any other material agreement to which Borrower is a party;\n\n**(i)** Payment by Borrower of the loan origination fee, all closing costs, and all legal fees and expenses of Lender's counsel, as described in Section 13;\n\n**(j)** Receipt by Lender of estoppel certificates from all existing tenants of the Property (Lowcountry Provisions Inc., Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC, and Tidemark Consulting Group LLC), dated no more than thirty (30) days prior to closing, in form and substance satisfactory to Lender;\n\n**(k)** Receipt by Lender of executed subordination, non-disturbance, and attornment agreements (\"SNDAs\") from all existing tenants of the Property, in form and substance satisfactory to Lender;\n\n**(l)** Delivery to Lender of a complete copy of the executed construction contract between Borrower and Beaufort Builders Group LLC, together with all schedules, exhibits, and amendments thereto;\n\n**(m)** Receipt by Lender of Borrower's equity contribution of Six Million Two Hundred Thousand Dollars (\\$6,200,000), or satisfactory evidence of the funding thereof, on or prior to the date of closing; and\n\n**(n)** Such other documents, certificates, instruments, agreements, and conditions as Lender or Lender's counsel may reasonably require.\n\n## SECTION 13: LOAN FEES AND EXPENSES\n\n### 13.1 Origination Fee\n\nBorrower shall pay to Lender, at closing, a loan origination fee equal to one percent (1.00%) of the total Loan Amount, in the amount of One Hundred Forty-Seven Thousand Five Hundred Dollars (\\$147,500). The origination fee shall be fully earned upon closing and shall not be refundable under any circumstances.\n\n### 13.2 Expenses\n\nBorrower shall pay all out-of-pocket costs and expenses incurred by Lender in connection with the origination, underwriting, documentation, closing, and administration of the Loan, including but not limited to:\n\n(a) legal fees and disbursements of Lender's counsel, Fielding, Ashworth & Cole LLP;\n\n(b) appraisal fees and any subsequent appraisal update or review fees;\n\n(c) environmental report fees, including the Phase I Environmental Site Assessment and any Phase II or supplemental assessments required by Lender;\n\n(d) title insurance premiums and title search charges;\n\n(e) ALTA/NSPS survey costs;\n\n(f) recording fees and documentary stamp taxes imposed by the State of South Carolina or Charleston County;\n\n(g) UCC filing and search fees;\n\n(h) ongoing construction inspection fees during the renovation period; and\n\n(i) such other costs and expenses as may be incurred by Lender in connection with the Loan.\n\n## SECTION 14: GOVERNING LAW AND MISCELLANEOUS\n\n### 14.1 Governing Law\n\nThe Loan Documents shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of South Carolina, without regard to principles of conflicts of law that would require the application of the laws of another jurisdiction. Any litigation arising out of or relating to this Term Sheet or the Loan Documents shall be brought in the courts of the State of South Carolina or the United States District Court for the District of South Carolina.\n\n### 14.2 Lender's Counsel\n\nLender's counsel for this transaction shall be **Fielding, Ashworth & Cole LLP**, with offices in Savannah, Georgia, and Charleston, South Carolina. Lead Partner: Catherine \"Kit\" Ashworth. Drafting Associate: Jordan Vickers. All Loan Documents shall be prepared by Lender's counsel, and all legal fees and expenses of Lender's counsel shall be paid by Borrower.\n\n### 14.3 Loan Documents\n\nThe following documents shall be prepared by Lender's counsel and executed and delivered at closing:\n\n(a) Promissory Note;\n\n(b) Mortgage and Security Agreement (to be recorded in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina);\n\n(c) Assignment of Leases and Rents (to be recorded, if prepared as a separate instrument from the Mortgage);\n\n(d) Environmental Indemnity Agreement;\n\n(e) Guaranty Agreement;\n\n(f) UCC-1 Financing Statement (to be filed with the South Carolina Secretary of State); and\n\n(g) Such other documents, instruments, certificates, and agreements as Lender or Lender's counsel may reasonably require.\n\nAll Loan Documents shall be in form and substance satisfactory to Lender and Lender's counsel in their sole discretion. In the event of any conflict between the terms of this Term Sheet and the terms of any Loan Document, the terms of the Loan Document shall control.\n\n### 14.4 Binding Nature\n\nThis Term Sheet, when executed by both Lender and Borrower, shall constitute a binding commitment of Lender to make the Loan upon the terms and conditions set forth herein, subject to: (a) completion of Lender's due diligence review to Lender's satisfaction; (b) preparation, execution, and delivery of the definitive Loan Documents; and (c) satisfaction of all conditions precedent to closing set forth in Section 12. Lender reserves the right to require additional provisions in the Loan Documents that are consistent with Lender's customary documentation requirements and applicable law and regulation, provided that such additional provisions are not materially inconsistent with the terms of this Term Sheet.\n\n### 14.5 Expiration\n\nThis commitment shall expire, and Lender's obligation to fund the Loan shall terminate, if closing does not occur on or before **May 15, 2025**, unless extended in writing by Lender in its sole discretion.\n\n### 14.6 Confidentiality\n\nThe terms and conditions of this Term Sheet are confidential and shall not be disclosed by either party to any third party without the prior written consent of the other party, except: (a) to such party's respective legal, financial, accounting, and tax advisors who have a need to know such information in connection with the Loan; (b) to the existing members of Borrower and their respective advisors; and (c) as may be required by applicable law, regulation, or court order.\n\n### 14.7 Counterparts\n\nThis Term Sheet may be executed in one or more counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original and all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument. Delivery of an executed signature page by facsimile or electronic mail (including PDF) shall have the same force and effect as delivery of an originally executed signature page.\n\n## SECTION 15: EXECUTION\n\n**IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the parties have executed this Term Sheet as of the date first set forth above.\n\n**AGREED AND ACCEPTED:**\n\n**LENDER:**\n\n**CALVERLEY HERITAGE BANK**\n\nBy: /s/ Marcus Prideaux Name: Marcus Prideaux Title: Senior Vice President -- Commercial Real Estate Lending Date: April 1, 2025\n\n**BORROWER:**\n\n**PALMETTO GATEWAY PARTNERS LLC** By: Graydon Development Group LLC, its Managing Member\n\nBy: /s/ Neil Ashford Graydon Name: Neil Ashford Graydon Title: Managing Member of Graydon Development Group LLC Date: April 1, 2025\n\n**GUARANTOR ACKNOWLEDGMENT:**\n\nThe undersigned Guarantor acknowledges the terms and conditions of this Term Sheet and agrees to execute the Guaranty Agreement, Completion Guaranty, Payment Guaranty, Environmental Indemnity Agreement, and all other guarantor documents described herein at or prior to closing.\n\nBy: /s/ Neil Ashford Graydon Neil Ashford Graydon, individually Date: April 1, 2025\n\n## EXHIBIT A\n\n**PROPERTY LEGAL DESCRIPTION (SUMMARY)**\n\nThe real property located at 520--534 King Street, Charleston, South Carolina 29403, and more particularly described as follows:\n\n**ALL** those certain lots, pieces, or parcels of land known and designated as **Lots 7, 8, and 9** of the Hampstead Village Plat, as recorded in Plat Book 41 at Page 218, in the Office of the Register of Mesne Conveyances (\"RMC Office\") for Charleston County, South Carolina;\n\n**TOGETHER WITH** that certain strip of land formerly known as Anson Lane, vacated by City of Charleston Ordinance No. 2019-084, and conveyed to the predecessor in title by that certain quitclaim deed recorded in Deed Book 1128 at Page 443 in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina;\n\n**BEING** the same property conveyed to Borrower by deed to be recorded simultaneously herewith in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina.\n\n**Tax Map Numbers:** 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009.\n\n*Full legal description to be confirmed from the title commitment (Commitment No. PT-2025-04-1178) and ALTA/NSPS Land Title Survey, and incorporated into the Mortgage and Security Agreement at closing.*\n\n## EXHIBIT B\n\n**RENOVATION BUDGET SUMMARY**\n\n  --------------------------------------------------------------\n  Line Item                       Budget Amount\n  ------------------------------- ------------------------------\n  HVAC Replacement                \\$1,200,000\n\n  Elevator Modernization          \\$475,000\n\n  Façade Restoration              \\$625,000\n\n  Tenant Improvement Allowances   \\$550,000\n\n  Soft Costs and Contingency      \\$300,000\n\n  **Total Renovation Budget**     **\\$3,150,000**\n  --------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  Funding Source                                    Amount\n  ------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------\n  Lender Renovation Holdback (from Loan proceeds)   \\$2,250,000\n\n  Borrower Equity for Renovation                    \\$900,000\n\n  **Total Renovation Funding**                      **\\$3,150,000**\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  Contract Reference                                                                        Amount\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------\n  GC Contract --- Beaufort Builders Group LLC (SC License No. SC-GC-47921) --- Hard Costs   \\$2,850,000\n\n  Soft Costs and Contingency (outside GC Contract)                                          \\$300,000\n\n  **Total**                                                                                 **\\$3,150,000**\n  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n*End of Term Sheet --- CHB CRE Loan No. 2025-CHS-0047*\n", "tool_call_id": "call_00_ET_UqzEcbi6Jbi7PQs1Qjnd9367", "tool_name": "read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"documents/executed-term-sheet.docx\"}"}
{"turn": 2, "role": "tool", "result": "**[COMMITMENT FOR TITLE INSURANCE]{.underline}**\n\n**Commonwealth National Title Underwriters Inc.**\n\nIssued by\n\n**Prestige Title & Settlement Services LLC** 120 Meeting Street Charleston, South Carolina 29401\n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Commitment No.:**                 **PT-2025-04-1178**\n  ----------------------------------- -----------------------------------\n  **Effective Date:**                 February 28, 2025, at 8:00 a.m.\n\n  **Commitment Expiration:**          August 28, 2025\n  -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCommonwealth National Title Underwriters Inc. (\\\"Company\\\"), a corporation organized and existing under the laws of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, hereby commits to issue its policy or policies of title insurance, as identified in Schedule A, in favor of the Proposed Insured named in Schedule A, subject to the provisions of Schedules A and B and to the Conditions of this Commitment. This Commitment is effective as of the Effective Date shown above for a period of six (6) months from such Effective Date (expiring August 28, 2025), unless extended by written endorsement executed by an authorized officer or agent of the Company.\n\nAll terms and conditions of the policy form(s) to be issued are incorporated herein by reference and shall be deemed a part of this Commitment.\n\nPRESTIGE TITLE & SETTLEMENT SERVICES LLC as Authorized Agent for Commonwealth National Title Underwriters Inc.\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Rebecca L. Hargrove, Esq.\n\nTitle: Title Officer\n\nDate: February 28, 2025\n\n**[CONDITIONS OF COMMITMENT]{.underline}**\n\n1\\. The Company will issue the Policy or Policies of title insurance described in Schedule A when it has been shown to the satisfaction of the Company that (a) the conditions set forth in Schedule B, Part I, have been met, and (b) the applicable premium, fees, and charges have been paid in full. The Company reserves the right to require additional information, instruments, or assurances prior to issuance of the Policy.\n\n2\\. This Commitment is preliminary to the issuance of a policy or policies of title insurance, and all liability and obligations of the Company hereunder shall cease and terminate six (6) months after the Effective Date set forth herein, or when the Policy is issued, whichever first occurs. If the Company\\'s liability and obligations cease and terminate under this paragraph, the Company\\'s only obligation shall be to return any fees paid for this Commitment that are required to be refunded under applicable state law.\n\n3\\. The liability of the Company under this Commitment shall not exceed the Proposed Policy Amount shown in Schedule A, and the liability of the Company shall be subject to and limited by the terms and provisions of the policy form to be issued, the Conditions of this Commitment, and the exceptions and exclusions set forth herein.\n\n4\\. This Commitment shall not be valid or binding until countersigned by a validly authorized officer or agent of the Company.\n\n5\\. The Company reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to amend, revise, supplement, or withdraw this Commitment at any time prior to issuance of the Policy upon discovery of any fact, circumstance, or matter not known to the Company as of the Effective Date, or upon any change in the condition of the title to the Land occurring after the Effective Date.\n\n6\\. This Commitment is issued in accordance with and subject to the provisions of the South Carolina Title Insurance Act, S.C. Code Ann. Section 38-75-10 *et seq.*, and the regulations promulgated thereunder by the South Carolina Department of Insurance, as the same may be amended from time to time.\n\n**[SCHEDULE A --- SUMMARY OF TRANSACTION AND PROPOSED POLICY]{.underline}**\n\n**Section 1: Effective Date and Commitment Number**\n\n  -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Effective Date of Commitment:**   **February 28, 2025, at 8:00 a.m.**\n  ----------------------------------- -------------------------------------\n  **Commitment No.:**                 PT-2025-04-1178\n\n  -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Section 2: Proposed Policy**\n\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Type of Policy:**                 **ALTA Loan Policy (06-17-06) with South Carolina modifications**\n  ----------------------------------- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  **Proposed Policy Amount:**         \\$14,750,000.00\n\n  **Proposed Insured:**               Calverley Heritage Bank, a Georgia state-chartered commercial bank, its successors and/or assigns\n\n  **Address of Proposed Insured:**    412 Whitaker Street, Savannah, GA 31401\n  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Section 3: Title to the Estate or Interest Covered**\n\n**Estate or Interest:** Fee Simple\n\nAt the Effective Date, title to the estate or interest in the land described in this Schedule A is vested in:\n\n**Hampstead Village Holdings LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company**, by virtue of that certain General Warranty Deed recorded on September 14, 2018, in Deed Book 1095 at Page 322, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina.\n\nALSO vested in Hampstead Village Holdings LLC by virtue of that certain Quitclaim Deed from the City of Charleston, recorded on March 22, 2019, in Deed Book 1128 at Page 443, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, conveying the vacated portion of Anson Lane pursuant to City of Charleston Ordinance No. 2019-084.\n\n*Note: Upon closing and recording of the instruments required in Schedule B, Part I, the Policy will be issued insuring title as vested in Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company, as the fee simple owner of the Land described herein, subject to the lien of the Mortgage in favor of the Proposed Insured.*\n\n**Section 4: Legal Description of the Land**\n\nThe land referred to in this Commitment is described as follows:\n\n**PARCEL ONE (Lots 7, 8, and 9):**\n\nALL that certain piece, parcel, or lot of land, together with any improvements thereon, situate, lying, and being in the City of Charleston, County of Charleston, State of South Carolina, being shown and designated as Lots 7, 8, and 9 of the Hampstead Village Plat, as recorded in Plat Book 41 at Page 218, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, and having such shapes, metes, bounds, and measurements as shown on said plat, reference to which is hereby made for a more complete and accurate description thereof.\n\nBeing commonly known as 520--534 King Street, Charleston, SC 29403.\n\nTax Map Nos.: 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009.\n\n**PARCEL TWO (Vacated Anson Lane Strip):**\n\nTOGETHER WITH that certain strip or parcel of land formerly constituting a portion of Anson Lane, a public street, which was vacated and closed by the City of Charleston pursuant to Ordinance No. 2019-084, and conveyed to the predecessor in title by that certain Quitclaim Deed recorded in Deed Book 1128 at Page 443, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, said strip being adjacent to and contiguous with Lot 7 of the Hampstead Village Plat, as more particularly described and shown on the plat prepared by Cartwright Land Surveying LLC dated January 15, 2025, recorded in Plat Book 64 at Page 91, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina.\n\n**[SCHEDULE B --- PART I: REQUIREMENTS]{.underline}**\n\nThe following requirements must be met prior to the issuance of the Policy or Policies described in Schedule A:\n\n**Requirement 1 --- Payment of Premium:**\n\nPayment to the Company of the full consideration for the policy or policies, together with all applicable recording fees, documentary stamp taxes, charges, and costs incurred in connection with the issuance thereof.\n\n**Requirement 2 --- Instruments Creating the Estate to Be Insured:**\n\nProper instrument(s) creating the estate or interest to be insured must be executed, delivered, and duly filed for record in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, including:\n\n> \\(a\\) A General Warranty Deed from Hampstead Village Holdings LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company, to Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company, conveying fee simple title to the Land described in Schedule A.\n\n**Requirement 3 --- Recording of the Mortgage and Security Agreement:**\n\nRecording in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, of a Mortgage and Security Agreement from Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC, a South Carolina limited liability company (\\\"Borrower\\\"), to Calverley Heritage Bank, a Georgia state-chartered commercial bank (\\\"Lender\\\"), in the principal amount of \\$14,750,000.00, encumbering the Land described in Schedule A, in form satisfactory to the Company.\n\n**Requirement 4 --- UCC-1 Financing Statement:**\n\nFiling of a UCC-1 Financing Statement with the South Carolina Secretary of State, naming Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC as Debtor and Calverley Heritage Bank as Secured Party, covering all fixtures and personal property located on or used in connection with the Land.\n\n**Requirement 5 --- Assignment of Leases and Rents:**\n\nDelivery and recording (if applicable) of an Assignment of Leases and Rents (or inclusion of an absolute assignment of rents within the Mortgage and Security Agreement) from Borrower to Lender, covering all existing and future leases affecting the Land, in form satisfactory to the Company.\n\n**Requirement 6 --- Environmental Indemnity Agreement:**\n\nDelivery of an Environmental Indemnity Agreement from Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC and Neil Ashford Graydon, individually, in favor of Calverley Heritage Bank, in form satisfactory to Lender, addressing environmental liabilities associated with the Land, including, without limitation, the Controlled Recognized Environmental Condition (CREC) identified in Clearfield Environmental Consulting LLC Phase I Environmental Site Assessment Report No. CLR-2025-0119, dated January 28, 2025, relating to the land use restriction recorded in Deed Book 1203 at Page 89 in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina. Such Environmental Indemnity Agreement shall specifically address the obligation to maintain and periodically inspect the vapor barrier beneath the ground-floor slab of Lot 7, and compliance with all terms and conditions of the SCDHEC land use restriction.\n\n**Requirement 7 --- Guaranty Agreement:**\n\nDelivery of a Guaranty Agreement from Neil Ashford Graydon, individually, of 14 Church Street, Charleston, SC 29401, in favor of Calverley Heritage Bank, guarantying the obligations of Borrower under the Mortgage and related loan documents.\n\n**Requirement 8 --- Evidence of Authority:**\n\nSatisfactory evidence that:\n\n> \\(a\\) Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC is a limited liability company duly organized, validly existing, and in good standing under the laws of the State of South Carolina (SC Secretary of State Filing No. 2024-0011287);\n>\n> \\(b\\) The person(s) executing the Mortgage and related loan documents on behalf of Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC are duly authorized to do so pursuant to the operating agreement and/or resolutions of the members of said company;\n>\n> \\(c\\) Graydon Development Group LLC, as Managing Member of Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC, is authorized to execute and deliver the Mortgage and all related loan documents on behalf of Borrower;\n>\n> \\(d\\) Hampstead Village Holdings LLC is duly authorized to convey the Land described in Schedule A.\n\n**Requirement 9 --- Survey:**\n\nDelivery of a current ALTA/NSPS Land Title Survey of the Land, certified to the Company, the Proposed Insured, and Borrower, prepared by a licensed South Carolina surveyor, dated or re-certified to a date not more than ninety (90) days prior to the date of closing, showing all improvements, encroachments, easements, rights-of-way, and other matters affecting the Land, and conforming to the 2021 Minimum Standard Detail Requirements for ALTA/NSPS Land Title Surveys.\n\n**Requirement 10 --- Tax Certificates:**\n\nEvidence that all real property taxes, assessments, and governmental charges affecting the Land for all years prior to 2025 have been paid in full, and that no delinquent taxes, tax liens, or pending tax sales exist with respect to the Land.\n\n**Requirement 11 --- Estoppel Certificates:**\n\nDelivery of tenant estoppel certificates from all tenants in occupancy at the Land, confirming the terms of their respective leases and the status of rental payments, security deposits, and landlord obligations, in form satisfactory to Lender.\n\n**Requirement 12 --- Additional Requirements:**\n\nSuch other instruments, documents, and assurances as the Company may reasonably require in connection with the issuance of the Policy, including but not limited to owner\\'s affidavits, gap indemnities, and lien waivers.\n\n**[SCHEDULE B --- PART II: EXCEPTIONS FROM COVERAGE]{.underline}**\n\nThe Policy or Policies to be issued will contain exceptions to the following matters unless the same are disposed of to the satisfaction of the Company:\n\n**Standard / General Exceptions**\n\n**Exception 1 --- Standard Printed Exceptions:**\n\nThe following standard exceptions will appear in the Policy unless removed by endorsement or satisfaction of applicable conditions prior to closing:\n\n> \\(a\\) Defects, liens, encumbrances, adverse claims, or other matters, if any, created, first appearing in the public records, or attaching subsequent to the Effective Date hereof but prior to the date the Proposed Insured acquires for value of record the estate or interest or mortgage thereon covered by this Commitment. *(Gap exception --- to be addressed by gap indemnity or disbursement at closing.)*\n>\n> \\(b\\) Any facts, rights, interests, or claims that are not shown by the public records but that could be ascertained by an inspection of the Land or by making inquiry of persons in possession thereof. *(To be deleted upon delivery of satisfactory survey and affidavit of possession.)*\n>\n> \\(c\\) Easements, liens, or encumbrances, or claims thereof, not shown by the public records. *(To be deleted upon delivery of satisfactory survey and owner\\'s affidavit.)*\n>\n> \\(d\\) Any encroachment, encumbrance, violation, variation, or adverse circumstance affecting the Title that would be disclosed by an accurate and complete land survey of the Land. *(To be deleted upon delivery of satisfactory ALTA/NSPS survey meeting the requirements of Requirement 9 above.)*\n>\n> \\(e\\) Any lien, or right to a lien, for services, labor, or material heretofore or hereafter furnished, imposed by law and not shown by the public records. *(To be deleted upon delivery of satisfactory affidavit and lien waiver, if applicable.)*\n\n**Specific Exceptions. Exception 2 --- Real Property Taxes for 2025:**\n\nReal property taxes for the year 2025, and all subsequent years, on Tax Map Nos. 460-12-04-007, 460-12-04-008, and 460-12-04-009, County of Charleston, State of South Carolina, a lien not yet due and payable.\n\n**Exception 3 --- Utility Easement (SC Electric & Gas):**\n\nEasement in favor of South Carolina Electric & Gas, a public utility, for the installation, maintenance, repair, and replacement of underground utility lines, as granted in that certain instrument recorded in Deed Book 987 at Page 112, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina. Said easement affects the westerly boundary of Lot 9 as shown on the Hampstead Village Plat.\n\n**Exception 4 --- SCDHEC Land Use Restriction (CREC --- Lot 7):**\n\nLand use restriction and institutional control recorded in Deed Book 1203 at Page 89, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, imposed by the South Carolina Department of Health and Environmental Control (SCDHEC), Site ID: SC-29403-0772, relating to environmental remediation of the adjacent property (518 King Street), which restriction:\n\n> \\(a\\) Prohibits the use of the ground floor of Lot 7 (Tax Map No. 460-12-04-007) for residential purposes; and\n>\n> \\(b\\) Requires the maintenance and periodic inspection of a vapor barrier beneath the slab of the ground-floor commercial space on Lot 7 (commonly known as Bay 1, 520 King Street).\n\nSaid restriction was imposed in connection with a \\\"No Further Action\\\" determination by SCDHEC dated August 12, 2021, and runs with the land. This exception will not be removed from the Policy. The Company makes no determination as to the current compliance status of this restriction.\n\n**Exception 5 --- Balcony Encroachment Over King Street Right-of-Way:**\n\nEncroachment of a decorative iron balcony, extending approximately two and one-half (2.5) feet beyond the front façade of the building situated on the Land, over and across the King Street public right-of-way, as shown on the ALTA/NSPS Land Title Survey prepared by Cartwright Land Surveying LLC, dated January 15, 2025. The Company makes no representation as to the existence, validity, or status of any permit, license, or encroachment agreement with the City of Charleston authorizing said encroachment. **NOTE: The Company recommends that the Proposed Insured obtain a survey/encroachment endorsement (ALTA Endorsement 28.1 or equivalent) if coverage over this matter is desired.**\n\n**Exception 6 --- Rights of Tenants in Possession:**\n\nRights of tenants under existing leases affecting the Land, as tenants only, without any option to purchase or right of first refusal to purchase the Land or any portion thereof, including but not limited to:\n\n> \\(a\\) Lowcountry Provisions Inc. --- Bay 1, 520 King Street (approximately 3,800 SF ground-floor retail);\n>\n> \\(b\\) Harmon & Wren Design Studio LLC --- Bay 3, 534 King Street (approximately 3,800 SF ground-floor retail);\n>\n> \\(c\\) Tidemark Consulting Group LLC --- 2nd Floor Suite A (approximately 9,800 SF office).\n\n**Note:** The Company has been advised that Bay 2 (approximately 3,800 SF ground-floor retail) and 2nd Floor Suite B (approximately 9,800 SF office) are currently vacant.\n\n**Exception 7 --- Miscellaneous Matters of Record:**\n\nAny and all matters shown on the plat recorded in Plat Book 41 at Page 218, in the RMC Office for Charleston County, South Carolina, including but not limited to setback lines, rights-of-way, drainage easements, and notations thereon.\n\n**[VESTING DEED INFORMATION / CHAIN OF TITLE NOTES]{.underline}**\n\n*(Informational Addendum --- Not Part of Commitment)*\n\n**Vesting Chain Summary (for informational purposes only):**\n\n1\\. **Lots 7, 8, and 9 (Parcel One):** Title to Lots 7, 8, and 9 of the Hampstead Village Plat is derived from a General Warranty Deed from Broad Street Property Ventures LLC to Hampstead Village Holdings LLC, dated September 10, 2018, recorded September 14, 2018, in Deed Book 1095 at Page 322, RMC Office for Charleston County. Prior vesting: General Warranty Deed from Coastal Palmetto Realty Trust to Broad Street Property Ventures LLC, dated April 3, 2009, recorded April 7, 2009, in Deed Book 934 at Page 157. The Company\\'s examination of the public records discloses an unbroken chain of general warranty deeds for Parcel One extending at least sixty (60) years.\n\n2\\. **Vacated Anson Lane Strip (Parcel Two):** Title to the vacated portion of Anson Lane is derived from a **Quitclaim Deed** from the City of Charleston to Hampstead Village Holdings LLC, dated February 28, 2019, recorded March 22, 2019, in Deed Book 1128 at Page 443, RMC Office for Charleston County. Said conveyance was made pursuant to City of Charleston Ordinance No. 2019-084, vacating and closing that portion of Anson Lane adjacent to Lot 7. **NOTE: This parcel was conveyed by Quitclaim Deed only. The Company has examined the public records and is satisfied that the City of Charleston held sufficient interest in Anson Lane to convey same; however, no warranties of title were provided in connection with this conveyance. The Company\\'s willingness to insure title to this parcel is based upon its examination of the municipal records and the recorded ordinance, and should not be construed as a representation that the chain of title for this parcel is equivalent to that of Parcel One.**\n\n**[NOTES AND SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO CLOSER]{.underline}**\n\nThe following notes are provided for the benefit of the Proposed Insured and its counsel in connection with the closing of this transaction:\n\n1\\. **Environmental Restriction (Exception 4):** Lender\\'s counsel should ensure that the Environmental Indemnity Agreement and the Mortgage and Security Agreement contain specific covenants addressing the SCDHEC land use restriction on Lot 7 (Deed Book 1203, Page 89), including the vapor barrier maintenance and periodic inspection obligation and the prohibition on residential use of the ground floor. This restriction runs with the land and cannot be removed without SCDHEC approval. The Mortgage should contain an event of default triggered by any failure to comply with or any modification, termination, or violation of said land use restriction.\n\n2\\. **Encroachment (Exception 5):** The Proposed Insured is advised to request a survey/encroachment endorsement (ALTA 28.1 or equivalent) to provide affirmative coverage over the balcony encroachment into the King Street right-of-way. Evidence of a valid encroachment permit or license from the City of Charleston should be obtained and reviewed prior to closing, if available. Absent such permit or license, the Proposed Insured should evaluate the risk of removal or modification of the encroaching structure by municipal authorities.\n\n3\\. **Anson Lane Strip (Parcel Two):** The Company will insure title to the vacated Anson Lane strip under the Policy; however, given the quitclaim conveyance, the Company reserves the right to require an additional premium for extended coverage on this parcel and/or may limit such coverage by endorsement. Lender\\'s counsel should confirm acceptability of coverage terms prior to closing and consider requesting an ALTA Endorsement 34 (Identified Exception) or other affirmative coverage specific to this parcel.\n\n4\\. **ALTA Survey:** The Company requires delivery of a current ALTA/NSPS survey conforming to the 2021 Minimum Standard Detail Requirements to remove standard exceptions (b), (c), (d), and (e) from Schedule B, Part II. The survey should show all improvements, including the decorative iron balcony described in Exception 5, and should include Table A items 1, 2, 3, 4, 6(a), 6(b), 8, 9, 11, 13, 14, 16, and 19.\n\n5\\. **Tenant Estoppel Certificates:** Required for all tenants in occupancy (see Exception 6) as a condition to issuance of the Policy. The Company does not insure against claims arising from undisclosed lease provisions or tenant rights not reflected in the public records.\n\n**[SIGNATURE / COUNTERSIGNATURE]{.underline}**\n\nISSUED BY:\n\nPRESTIGE TITLE & SETTLEMENT SERVICES LLC as Authorized Agent for Commonwealth National Title Underwriters Inc.\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: Rebecca L. Hargrove, Esq.\n\nTitle: Title Officer\n\nDate: February 28, 2025\n\n120 Meeting Street Charleston, South Carolina 29401 Telephone: (843) 555-0147\n\nEmail: rhargrove@prestigetitlesc.com\n\nAgent License No.: SC-TA-2019-04882\n\nCOUNTERSIGNED:\n\nCOMMONWEALTH NATIONAL TITLE UNDERWRITERS INC.\n\nBy: **\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\nName: David R. Stonebridge\n\nTitle: Vice President --- Southeastern Division\n\nDate: February 28, 2025\n\n*--- End of Commitment ---*\n", "tool_call_id": "call_01_ET_zHx26ZYBbM8YSzjk2iYp9043", "tool_name": "read", "arguments": "{\"file_path\": \"documents/title-commitment.docx\"}"}
