{"turn": 73, "role": "assistant", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_00_ET_XYMH9nUmbtXLudw4Wh7E5933", "name": "finish", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Drafted a recordable South Carolina Mortgage and Security Agreement and an accompanying drafting-issues memorandum for the $14,750,000 Calverley Heritage Bank / Palmetto Gateway Partners LLC loan on 520–534 King Street, Charleston.\\n\\n**Mortgage and Security Agreement** (~24,200 words, 63 pp.): 13 Articles / 98 Sections with static table of contents, six Exhibits, signature page with two subscribing witnesses and a South Carolina notarial acknowledgment, and a guarantor limited joinder. Substantively it delivers the three structural instructions from prior counsel: absolute (not collateral) assignment of leases and rents incorporated into the mortgage body under the South Carolina Uniform Assignment of Rents Act; a genuinely enforceable single-purpose-entity package with independent manager, separateness covenants and bankruptcy remoteness; and a self-contained, mathematically determinate yield maintenance formula using Federal Reserve H.15 with interpolation. It also answers the title commitment's instructions to closer by adding dedicated SCDHEC land-use-restriction and vapor-barrier covenants with their own Event of Default, states expressly that foreclosure is judicial only with no power of sale, and includes ALTA 34/28.1/19/17/14 endorsement requirements for the quitclaim Anson Lane parcel and the balcony encroachment.\\n\\n**Issues Memorandum** (~14,300 words, 30 pp.): risk-prioritised top-risk register (24 entries), a 30-issue log stating finding / drafting treatment / required action, an independent recomputation worksheet of every material figure, an 18-item open-items and diligence table with owners and CP flags, a closing-condition matrix against Term Sheet §12, a term-sheet-to-mortgage traceability table, drafting decisions with alternatives, and limitations.\\n\\nSource reconciliation surfaced four critical findings: (1) the DSCR covenant is unattainable — best-case 0.554x and realistic 0.280x against 1.25x required, which needs NOI of $1,405,299 versus $622,772 projected; (2) the appraisal's income approach yields $5.3–10.1m, not the $18.2m/$23.5m concluded, so the 81.04% as-is LTV rests on sales comparison alone; (3) occupancy is 56.13%, not the 68% recited in both the term sheet and appraisal, whose own area figures total 35,000 SF in a 31,000 SF building; (4) the operating agreement cannot support a non-recourse loan and requires an amendment signed by all three members because a 72% managing member cannot meet the 75% Major Decisions threshold. Eleven further high-rated issues include the Anson Lane quitclaim coverage, the environmental covenants (where prior counsel's \\\"standard provisions suffice\\\" conflicts with Title Requirement 6), the guaranty's 14-month window expiring before the DSCR test, and a sources-and-uses gap leaving ~$202,075 of known closing costs unfunded. The worksheet also catches draw-schedule errors (equity over-drawn by $5,000; $50,000 misallocated between HVAC and elevator; retainage unmodelled). Unresolvable items — metes and bounds, unredacted operating agreement, construction contract, leases, guarantor financials, Harborline ownership — are expressly flagged rather than invented.\\n\\nBoth .docx files pass the docx validation gate and render correctly to PDF.\", \"deliverables\": [\"mortgage-and-security-agreement.docx\", \"drafting-issues-memorandum.docx\", \"response.md\"]}"}], "input_tokens": 273916, "output_tokens": 790, "finish_reason": "completed"}
